WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.533 --> 00:00:10.348
Marcus Bell: Hey Ashley, how's it going? Sorry, I think I'm... there we go. Can you hear me okay?

2
00:00:10.756 --> 00:00:18.246
Ashley Moore: Hey Marcus. Yeah, loud and clear. I'm in the truck today, so if it sounds weird it's just the road.

3
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:23.968
Marcus Bell: No worries. Are you driving? We can push this if that's easier.

4
00:00:25.265 --> 00:00:31.804
Ashley Moore: No no, I'm parked. Just finished dropping flyers at the Durham office. It's It's fine.

5
00:00:32.641 --> 00:00:40.493
Marcus Bell: Okay good. How's October treating you? I mean, I saw your call volume ticked up a bit versus September.

6
00:00:41.664 --> 00:00:54.289
Ashley Moore: Yeah, we're up, um... I want to say 11 percent. Fall is always busy for us, people want the lawn treatments before winter and then the pest side picks up when everything comes inside.

7
00:00:55.334 --> 00:01:03.830
Marcus Bell: Makes sense. Anything weird in the data on your end? I noticed the Raleigh number had a couple of quiet days last week.

8
00:01:04.155 --> 00:01:14.939
Ashley Moore: Uh, Oh, um, that was just Darnell out sick and then, you know, we had two techs at that training in Charlotte, so the routing was a little thin Tuesday and Wednesday.

9
00:01:14.939 --> 00:01:16.287
Ashley Moore: Back to normal now.

10
00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:24.797
Marcus Bell: Got it. Speaking of which, I wanted to check in on a couple of things before your campaign review next month.

11
00:01:24.797 --> 00:01:26.824
Marcus Bell: How's the Google Ads side looking?

12
00:01:28.028 --> 00:01:32.276
Ashley Moore: It's fine. Conversions are flowing. Nothing's broken, which is nice for once.

13
00:01:33.297 --> 00:01:35.775
Marcus Bell: Good. So what's on your mind?

14
00:01:37.215 --> 00:01:46.646
Ashley Moore: Two things. Um, the first one, honestly, is that I keep getting emails from a CallRail rep. Like, four in the last two weeks.

15
00:01:46.646 --> 00:02:03.543
Ashley Moore: And the pitch is always the same, same-day conversion sync to Google Ads. They're saying we're losing bidding time, that if a call comes in at 2pm the conversion doesn't hit Ads until the next day so we're basically bidding on yesterday's information.

16
00:02:04.856 --> 00:02:09.080
Marcus Bell: Okay. And is that... are they quoting you anything specific?

17
00:02:09.758 --> 00:02:18.243
Ashley Moore: They came in about 20 percent under our current spend. Which, you know, I'm not going to pretend that doesn't get my attention.

18
00:02:18.243 --> 00:02:24.514
Ashley Moore: Colby, our owner, he forwards me their emails now. He doesn't even say anything, just forwards them.

19
00:02:25.008 --> 00:02:34.122
Marcus Bell: That's fair. I'd rather hear it from you than find out later. Can you forward me the last one or two?

20
00:02:34.122 --> 00:02:52.784
Marcus Bell: I'm not going to promise anything on pricing in this call, but I want to make sure whoever needs to see it does, and I can at least get you a clear answer on what the sync timing actually is on our side.

21
00:02:53.498 --> 00:03:04.981
Ashley Moore: Yeah, I'll send them over. It's not like we're unhappy, it's just... you know how it it is. Um, when um, the owner forwards you an email he's asking a question.

22
00:03:05.394 --> 00:03:09.807
Marcus Bell: Totally. And you own Google Ads in-house, right? Nobody else touches it?

23
00:03:10.528 --> 00:03:13.943
Ashley Moore: Just me. Which is the other thing, actually.

24
00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:15.310
Marcus Bell: Go ahead.

25
00:03:15.816 --> 00:03:31.856
Ashley Moore: So the spam flagging in Signal AI. It's marking real customers as spam. I was pulling the October numbers Monday and we're down, and I'm sitting there thinking, we are not down, the phones have not stopped ringing.

26
00:03:31.856 --> 00:03:41.142
Ashley Moore: So So I start reading transcripts. And there's this one, Saturday morning, 7:40. Caller says the street address, that's it. Eleven seconds.

27
00:03:41.142 --> 00:03:49.161
Ashley Moore: Flagged as spam. That's a real person, Marcus. That's somebody standing in their yard looking at the wasp nest.

28
00:03:49.634 --> 00:03:54.894
Marcus Bell: Okay. So it's the short ones where they just give you the address.

29
00:03:56.212 --> 00:04:08.956
Ashley Moore: That's the pattern I'm seeing, yeah. Short calls, weekend, after hours, caller uh, gives an address and hangs up. The The system seems to think it's a robocall or a survey or something.

30
00:04:08.956 --> 00:04:17.838
Ashley Moore: And it's not ten calls, it's more like 30 or 40 this month across the six locations, and those just vanish from reporting.

31
00:04:17.838 --> 00:04:25.561
Ashley Moore: So my cost per lead looks worse than it is and I look like I don't know what I'm doing.

32
00:04:26.301 --> 00:04:30.614
Marcus Bell: How are you catching them? Are you reading through transcripts one by one?

33
00:04:31.571 --> 00:04:41.070
Ashley Moore: I filtered by spam and by call duration under 30 seconds, and then just, so, yeah, read them. It took me most of Monday afternoon.

34
00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:49.049
Ashley Moore: I only found it because a customer called back Tuesday and was annoyed nobody had followed up on her Saturday message.

35
00:04:50.228 --> 00:04:57.782
Marcus Bell: Okay. I want to get this in front of the right folks. Can you send me three or four call IDs?

36
00:04:57.782 --> 00:05:03.537
Marcus Bell: The weekend ones especially, and the one where she called back, if you have it it.

37
00:05:04.858 --> 00:05:10.981
Ashley Moore: I can do like, that today. I already have a little list in a spreadsheet.

38
00:05:12.162 --> 00:05:20.456
Marcus Bell: Perfect. I don't have an answer for you on this call, and I'm not going to guess at why it's happening.

39
00:05:20.456 --> 00:05:28.749
Marcus Bell: I'll take the examples, get them to the team, and come back to you with what they say and a timeline.

40
00:05:29.975 --> 00:05:34.239
Ashley Moore: That's all I need. Um, I just don't want it to sit.

41
00:05:34.516 --> 00:05:38.237
Marcus Bell: It won't. Anything else, or is that the list?

42
00:05:38.456 --> 00:05:46.162
Ashley Moore: That's the list. Everything else is quiet. Numbers are tracking right, the campaigns are set up the way we talked about in August.

43
00:05:46.521 --> 00:05:56.183
Marcus Bell: Good. One logistics thing, your campaign review is the first week of November, I'm thinking Tuesday the 3rd. Does 2pm work, or is that school pickup?

44
00:05:57.247 --> 00:06:02.592
Ashley Moore: Ha, uh, 2pm is fine, pickup's at 3:15. Tuesday the 3rd, put it on the calendar.

45
00:06:03.259 --> 00:06:10.433
Marcus Bell: Done. And I'll send you a note after this with the call ID format so you know exactly what to pull.

46
00:06:11.501 --> 00:06:22.065
Ashley Moore: Great. Hey, I'm going to run, I've got a tech waiting on me about a truck. Thanks for listening on the spam thing, seriously.

47
00:06:23.553 --> 00:06:28.408
Marcus Bell: Of course. Send those over when you get a chance. Talk soon, Ashley.

48
00:06:29.534 --> 00:06:30.900
Ashley Moore: Will do. Bye Marcus.
